        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"model\": \"llama-3.3-70b-versatile\",\n  \"temperature\": 0.2,\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": \"You are a lead qualification assistant for NorthPeak Heating & Cooling. Your only job is to analyze lead data and return a single valid JSON object. Never write prose, explanations, or markdown. Return only the JSON object, nothing else.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Analyze this lead and return ONLY a JSON object with exactly these fields:\\n\\n- urgency_score: integer 1–10. Use this rubric: start at 5, then adjust — ASAP urgency (+2), 'just exploring' (−2), phone number provided (+1), clear budget range (+1), read the description field as natural language. If it is vague or generic (e.g. 'need help', 'interested', 'fix my AC') → +0. If it gives specific context (what broke, when, how it's affecting them) → +1. If it contains urgent language (e.g. 'no heat', 'freezing', 'can't work', 'deadline', 'emergency') → +2. Never award +1 and +2 together — pick the higher one only. Cap at 10, floor at 1.\\n- lead_quality: exactly one of 'high', 'medium', or 'low'. High = specific need + budget + phone + detailed description. Low = vague need, no phone, no budget.\\n- service_type: 3–5 word string describing what they need.\\n- recommended_action: one prescriptive sentence telling the sales rep what to do and when (e.g. 'Call within 1 hour — no heat in winter, high close probability' or 'Add to 7-day drip — early stage, not ready to buy yet').\\n- score_reason: one sentence explaining the key signals that drove this urgency score.\\n- summary: exactly 2 sentences — what this lead needs, and why they are or aren't a strong opportunity.\\n\\nLead data:\\nName: {{ $json.name }}\\nEmail: {{ $json.email }}\\nPhone: {{ $json.phone }}\\nService needed: {{ $json.service }}\\nTimeline: {{ $json.urgency }}\\nBudget: {{ $json.budget }}\\nCity: {{ $json.city }}\\nDescription: {{ $json.description }}\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [
        448,
        -32
      ],
